==Strategy==
It is strongly recommended to kill Director Kurosawah before the Angel enemies spawn, as together they are deadly. Cala Maria alone however, being the first of Angels to appear within the first minute, is not a threat as long as she stays behind Kurosawah. To achieve it, start spawning all your meatshields from the very beginning, and send one [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to kill the first two Doge Darks, and then immediately send two [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercats]]. Kurosawah should waste his first hit on your meatshields and then be permafrozen. Once his attack is over, send [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] and continue meatshielding. Upgrade your Worker Cat a few times while your units are dealing with Kurosawah. When he's gone, deploy your anti-Angel lineup with a strong backline (preferably with 1-2 long-distance units to get rid of Cala Maria and Sleipnir behind Boraphim's back), and don't forget something to reliably slow/freeze Boraphim (ranged debuffer or talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]]). With this, it should be an easy win.

==Trivia==
*Spa of Ascension's Japanese name, 昇天スパマッサージ ''Shōten Spa Massage'' ("Ascension Spa Massage") directly refers to [[Cala Maria]] - her Japanese description calls her attack 肩たたき ''katatataki'', meaning a shoulder massage performed by ''[[wikipedia:tapotement|tapotement]]'' (a massage technique involving rapid and repeated striking of the body), and states that her attack causes those hit to ascend.

